meantime a new report has found  two-thirds of people are concerned about  the cost of Christmas dinner this year  amid the cost of living crisis a survey  by the Salvation Army also found almost  one in five people expect to use items  from a food bank this festive season can  you believe that let's speak now to  Lieutenant Colonel Fallon from the  Salvation Army with us here in the  studio hi Dean it's good to see you  thanks so much indeed for joining us on  the program this morning one in five  people using a food bank that's what our  server has shown and it mirrors what  we're seeing on the ground a huge  increase in the number of people coming  to us for food food parcels and and  other support and people who would never  have normally expected to come to the  Salvation Army we're seeing nurses  coming to our food banks we are seeing  people who are just saying I used to  donate to you thank you very much for  the support you can give and that's  great we want people to come but there  is an incredibly high level of anxiety I  think it's 80 percent of people over 65  are saying they're not sure how they can  afford Christmas dinner and so yes  there's a problem and there's also a  significant level of stress and worry  out there about about the economic  situation and personal finance because I  mean it's December this the  week you know Christmas is just a month  away and normally we get so excited  about Christmas you know all the family  around the table lots of presents under  the tree that's not going to be the case  for a lot of people no we I heard a  heartbreaking story recently of a man  who's been told by his family we can't  afford you to come this Christmas and he  was saying I'm going to stay home and I  think the message to people like that is  please don't stay at home there are  there are churches like the Salvation  Army there are Charities there are other  faiths who want to welcome you in and  we're also part of the warm welcome  campaign of saying to people if you want  a warm place to come a place where  you'll be welcome and be made to feel at  home come come to the Salvation Army or  come to to one of the other places  around the around the country so I think  we're trying to reach out to people but  also to thank people who are our  financial supporters who help us to do  this work because that's also difficult  for people at this time when everybody's  under economic pressure at the moment so  what do people do if they feel Under  Pressure they don't know what to do they  don't know they're being told not to go  to the family because they can't afford  them to be around the table how do you  help them what do you do so we partner  with other people the Salvation armies  in 600 places across communities across  the country with our churches and our  community centers we've also got a  network of lifehouses for people who are  homeless and so we reach out to the most  vulnerable people on the streets but we  like working Partnerships so in your  town in your city in your neighborhood  you'll find someone you'll find a church  you'll find a community group you may  find the Salvation Army go and talk to  them we're not McDonald's we don't do  everything the same across the country  but reach out and people really want to  connect with you and try and help  everybody through this Christmas season  what about people who say I'm not  religious I can't I can't ask for for  any help from the Salvation Army yeah we  we've been around 155 years and we look  after people irrespective of religion  and yes Christmas is a Christian season  and it's a celebration and we want it to  be joyful we want people to celebrate  the birth of Jesus but everybody is  welcome and and there's no pressure  um certainly you know there's a cup of  tea a bit of cake or whatever it is  you'll be very very welcome  going to food banks because I I know  from my own experience of you know  working in them people are embarrassed  and they don't want to do it yep  we really don't just want to hand out  food we want a relationship with someone  we want to try and find out how can we  help you know the Salvation Army's also  got Employment Services to help people  get work debt to help you if you've got  your financial problems so it's all  sorts of wrap around services or we can  refer you to other partners in in your  community who can help so I think it's  it's if you're facing difficulty it  might be that we can give you a  Christmas toy for your children this  year reach out see how we can work  together with you and and in a  partnership I think we can solve this  and people who want to support the  Salvation Army how do they do that our  website  salvationarmy.org.uk we've delighted to  receive donations thank you very much  okay it's good to see you Merry  Christmas maybe a little bit earlier  thank you nice to see you thank you very  much thank you
 

